.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt PKG-FORMAT 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg-format
.Nd the Novi package format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ar name Ns - Ns Ar version Ns - Ns Ar arch Ns .pkg.tar.gz
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A Novi package is a gzipped tar archive holding a
.Pa MANIFEST ,
a
.Pa files/
tree that mirrors the root filesystem, and optionally a
.Pa scripts/
directory.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
MANIFEST
files/usr/bin/curl
files/usr/lib/libcurl.so.4
scripts/post-install
.Ed
.Ss MANIFEST
Lines of
.Ar field Ns = Ns Ar value .
Required:
.Bl -tag -width "description" -compact
.It Va name
Lowercase, no spaces.
.It Va version
.It Va arch
.It Va description
One line.
.El
.Pp
Optional:
.Bl -tag -width "replaces-files"
.It Va depends
.Sy Comma Ns -separated
package names.
Not spaces \(em
mkpkg(1)
refuses a space outright, because a package written from the wrong
belief builds, indexes and signs perfectly and then fails at install
naming the whole list as one imaginary package.
.It Va replaces-files
Space-separated root-relative paths this package knowingly takes over
from
.Em no other package .
.It Va size
Installed size in KB.
Set by
mkpkg(1).
.It Va url
.It Va license
An SPDX identifier.
.It Va maintainer
.El
.Pp
.Va provides ,
.Va conflicts
and
.Va replaces
appear in the spec and are
.Sy not implemented .
Note that
.Va replaces
is
.Em not
.Va replaces-files :
the first is the conventional dpkg meaning and does nothing here.
.Ss Who owns a file
.Xr pkg 1
refuses to install a path another package owns, refuses a path
.Em nothing
owns, and takes over an unowned one only on an explicit
.Va replaces-files= .
The original is saved, so
.Nm pkg remove
puts it back \(em which is the whole reason a declared takeover is
worth having.
The harm was never the overwrite; it was that the machine could not
be put back.
.Pp
.Fl -overwrite
is the operator's answer to whatever is in the way, and deliberately
not something a MANIFEST can ask for.
.Ss Lifecycle scripts
Each runs as root with
.Ar name Ar version
as its arguments.
.Bl -column -offset indent "post-install" "aborts the install"
.It Sy script Ta Sy a failure
.It Pa pre-install Ta Sy aborts the install
.It Pa post-install Ta warns; the install stands
.It Pa pre-remove Ta warns; removal proceeds
.It Pa post-remove Ta warns; removal stands
.El
.Pp
Only
.Pa pre-install
is fatal, and that is the design: it runs before anything has moved,
so refusing leaves the machine exactly as it was.
The other three run once files are already on or off the disk, where
aborting would leave a half-installed package \(em worse than either
outcome.
.Pp
.Sy A script runs unattended, as root, at boot .
.Va packages.\& Ns Ar name
means boot convergence can install a package.
Prefer shipping a file to running code, and keep what runs
idempotent, because an upgrade runs it again.
.Ss Trust
The repository index is signed once, with Ed25519, and every
package's SHA-256 is inside it.
.Nm pkg sync
verifies the signature with
.Xr novi-verify 1
before believing a line;
.Nm pkg install
re-checks each archive's hash before unpacking,
.Em cached archives included .
.Pp
The index format forbids
.Ql \&|
in every field rather than escaping it: an escaping scheme in a
format parsed by
.Ic read
is a bug waiting to happen.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/lib/pkg/installed/<name>" -compact
.It Pa /var/lib/pkg/installed/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /MANIFEST
.It Pa /var/lib/pkg/installed/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /FILES
.It Pa /var/lib/pkg/installed/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /scripts/
Copied in, because
.Pa pre-remove
runs long after the archive is gone.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr novi-verify 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr pkg.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0006, RFC 0040.
.Sh CAVEATS
Version comparison is
.Nm sort Fl V ,
never a string equality: a string comparison says 1.9.2 is newer than
1.10.0, which is the kind of wrong that ships a downgrade.
